fuxi: 0130 -- declare vsnprintf so RELEASE builds compile

0121's panic note calls vsnprintf, which no kernel header declares: DEVELOPMENT builds
accepted it through a different include path, RELEASE fails with "call to undeclared
function 'vsnprintf'" and the build dies at debug.c:996.  Other kernel files (osfmk/tests)
declare it inline for the same reason; do the same.

This is what blocks any optimisation comparison that needs a RELEASE kernel.

Harness: applied=129 skipped=0.
--- a/osfmk/kern/debug.c
+++ b/osfmk/kern/debug.c
@@ -985,6 +985,8 @@
 	 */
 	{
 		extern void fuxi_log_panic_note(const char *text);
+		/* No kernel header declares this; RELEASE builds reject implicit decls. */
+		extern int vsnprintf(char *, size_t, const char *, va_list);
 		static bool fuxi_panic_note_busy;
 		va_list fuxi_copy;
 		char fuxi_msg[224];
